      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (as documented in [[write-journal]]) describes a mechanism that records file state before any write happens, enabling rollback on failure.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n1. **Prior state recording**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s previous state \u2014 either its prior content (if it existed) or a note that it did not exist.\n\n2. **In-memory transaction log**: This prior state is stored in an in-memory write journal that acts as a transaction log for the duration of a single agent run.\n\n3. **Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal rolls back every recorded write in reverse order \u2014 restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n\n4. **All-or-nothing semantics**: This approach gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without needing a database transaction \u2014 the in-process journal itself provides transactional guarantees.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback path, since it has no write tool at all.",
      "input_tokens": 5354,
      "output_tokens": 261
    }
